  "summary": "Round 3's items are fixed. The orchestral F5-C5 run at 15.65-16.92 is deleted, so 15.3-19.05 is silent like the band intro, n29 now starts at the 25.80 swoop and n25 runs to 22.05. The whistle line holds up: the 14.73 pickup (G#6 F#6 D#6), the 19.1-22.05 phrase with its correct steps (n24 is a stable C7 after a scoop, n25 is C#7), the soft G7/F#7/D#7 traces at 22.7-24.6, and the 24.87-28.6 phrase (A#6 chirp, C#7, A6, G6, C7, A6, C7, G6, B6, C7, A6, B6, C7). Every remaining diff is speech (0-8 s), orchestra, bleed, or a glide or contour limit on a flagged note. The slow C7-to-G7 gliss at 20.2-20.7 (n54) and the 25.8 swoop (n29) are flagged genuine ambiguities. The faint wavering ~G7-G#7 lines at 29.0-29.9 come with parallel high partials, have no attack of their own and sit over a sustained C7 orchestral chord, so they are read as accompaniment, not a missing whistle note. Minor non-blocking offset notes: n24 could run to the n25 onset at 21.85 (the original stays voiced through the gap), and the rising tails after n19 (to about 19.72) and n57 (to about 28.75) could be folded into those notes' offsets.",
